{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches","id":64073,"title":"A couple questions about Fetches....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-03T09:35:43-08:00","id":64073,"title":"A couple questions about Fetches....","content":"So, can fetches be possessed? As in by spirits, ghosts,whatever with the possessions.<br /> <br /> Also, if say a fetch wanted to become Human, is there some way it could go about it? Was thinking about having a Fetch NPC ask my characters for help.... help finding Prometheans specifically, so if could get Pyros from them, or otherwise find out how they quest for a soul of their own, see if it can do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/906-qoorl","name":"Qoorl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:25:53-08:00","id":64110,"title":"","content":"Fetches are immune to spiritual possession.<br /> <br /> Prometheans can become human. Fetches cannot.<br /> <br /> You can obviously make up your own system for it, but using the books that's what you get. Prometheans are pilgrims. Fetches are placeholders.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be an appropriate story for a fetch to torment Prometheans thinking they could somehow fix them? Or go on a long quest for a soul of their own and fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:26:48-08:00","id":64150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Qoorl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches#post64073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, if say a fetch wanted to become Human, is there some way it could go about it?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches?p=64110#post64110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fetches are placeholders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to point out: 90-95% of fetches already think they are human (and probably more, considering the below); only 5-10% of changelings return from Arcadia, so most fetches will never really have an occasion to even consider their non-humanness. Additionally, most wouldn't necessarily just automatically assume the changeling is the real person and they themselves are the copy. I mean, if you remember everything you did from being a small child to the present and some deformed sort-of version of you showed up, claiming that <i>they </i>were the real you, abducted by extra-dimensional faeries, escaped, and that <i>you </i>were just a trash-poppet stand-in, would your reaction be &quot;You know, you are right! I am just a souless husk. You are definitely the real person. Emo-angst, here I come!&quot;? Because most people would beat the sideshow freak to death, hide the corpse, and go home and bang the wife senseless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1651-phalamir","name":"phalamir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T17:43:30-08:00","id":64457,"title":"","content":"A good chunk of Fetches know they're fakes from the moment of their creation. It's never specified how many, but I don't recall anything saying it's more or less common than Fetches thinking they're human. It's entirely up to the Fae that makes them, and the Fae are hardly reliable or formulaic in how they operate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T19:24:57-08:00","id":64509,"title":"","content":"Qoorl,<br /> Assuming you follow the rules as stated by nofather, would you consider making your NPC a Promethean that has some crossed wires (so to speak) and believes he is a Fetch? The players would then have the opportunity to help make the NPC real, probably by revealing the NPC's true nature to itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T05:41:46-08:00","id":64766,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Probably just going to bend the rules. Actually I guess I already have. The chronicle started with the characters in the first year of High School, and has progressed from there. The Fetch in question was one of their high school friends. During the course of the game, the fetch's changeling came back, tried to hunt the fetch down. The characters eventually helped them work out an accord and they had a pretty tenuous truce. Last session I ran a modified version of the hunter SAS Under the Skin. The fetch ended up being possessed by Wastes of Civilization. She had gone to the doctor, learned she was barren, realized that it was because she wasn't a real human. Her disgust and shame at her condition made her ripe for WoC to possess her. They freed her and now she's going to try and convince the troupe to see if they can find a way for her to be a real human, I've decided in my world at least, spirits can go into fetch's easier than humans because they're basically empty shells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/906-qoorl","name":"Qoorl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T09:49:53-08:00","id":67957,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there hints that Fetches and Lost could merge into one whole being? What if a self aware Fetch hears these stories and thinks it's their path to becoming a real boy, and sets out on a grand quest to rescue their other half from the clutches of their creator? Perhaps said Fetch would seek out Lost that have already escaped their master to help there quest along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Khan shot first!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1781-ajaba-the-hut","name":"Ajaba the Hut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1781_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:46:25-08:00","id":68056,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything wrong with Fetches becoming real boys through the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:47:02-08:00","id":68058,"title":"","content":"And where did it say Fetches can't be possessed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T21:12:19-08:00","id":68236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches?p=68056#post68056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see anything wrong with Fetches becoming real boys through the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It kind of undermines the entire theme of Fetches as doppelgangers. The whole point is that Fetches aren't real humans and they never can be. They're a soulless simulacrum of a real person, because the Fae cannot create, they can only mimic, modify or copy. The only thing that gives them a spark of life is having a scrap of the soul of the person they're a copy of ripped out of the original and attached to the doppelganger so that it can fool the world for 'long enough'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T23:45:59-08:00","id":68275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches?p=68236#post68236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It kind of undermines the entire theme of Fetches as doppelgangers. The whole point is that Fetches aren't real humans and they never can be. They're a soulless simulacrum of a real person, because the Fae cannot create, they can only mimic, modify or copy. The only thing that gives them a spark of life is having a scrap of the soul of the person they're a copy of ripped out of the original and attached to the doppelganger so that it can fool the world for 'long enough'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it? I personally think that a fetch's option to drop the pretenses of a false life in search of a new one is very well suited considering Changeling's theme of finding one's home.<br /> <br /> The only issue at hand is that runs headlong into the theme and mechanics of another game and apparently people don't like crossing the streams with it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-09T00:48:21-08:00","id":68287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches?p=68058#post68058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And where did it say Fetches can't be possessed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Autumn Nightmares, the chapter dealing with fetches, where specifically it says, 'Fetches are immune to spiritual possession'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/64073-a-couple-questions-about-fetches?p=68275#post68275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and apparently people don't like crossing the streams with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see this kind of thing a lot. It's quite unfair. Everyone knows you can do whatever you want. That's implicit. The problem is, when people ask 'Can you do this,' the answer is always yes. So we take for granted that when people ask questions like these, they are asking if there are rules allowing them. Because everyone knows if you're just doing it yourself, the answer is always yes, anything is possible, mixing templates, fetches being vampire-werewolf-solar exalts is perfectly fine in your own game.<br /> <br /> But in terms of the books published, fetches cannot become Prometheans. This isn't about people liking it or not or not liking how you run or play things, cause unless those people are co-storytelling at your table, none of that matters. Eldagusto has fetches part of a freehold alongside changelings, I've thrown an Exalted into a vampire game and I know of many people who mix and match aspects of cWoD into their nWoD games. The only people who have a say on what goes on at your table are the people who play at your table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-09-2014, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}